WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.509
Sheep in press vests outside the offices of
Novaya Gazeta in Moscow.

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:08.290
The display might look cute, but it's no petting
zoo.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:13.110
Instead, its part of the latest scare campaign
against the opposition newspaper.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:18.089
Just a few days before, the journalists received
a severed sheep's head and a funeral wreath

00:00:18.089 --> 00:00:21.510
addressed to the editor-in-chief and the journalist
Denis Korotkov.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:27.550
Korotkov has worked for Novaya Gazeta from
St. Petersburg since September.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:31.669
Even in this Café in the center of the city
he worries about surveillance.

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:34.570
On the internet he has been accused of being
a traitor.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:39.000
The wave of online hate is connected to his
investigation into the dealings of Putin's

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.840
cohort Evgeny Prigozhin.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.670
He is allegedly behind the so-called troll
factory, which pays people to promote the

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.720
Kremlin's interests online - and behind a
controversial Russian mercenary group.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:58.900
"They put my addresses on the internet, information
about my relatives, about members of my family

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:05.220
- and they openly discuss online about what
to do to me.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.190
Can I say that I find that pleasant and enjoyable?

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.400
Of course I don’t.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.920
But do I feel a certain satisfaction, because
these threats mean that I wrote the right

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:16.920
thing?

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:17.920
Yes."

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.270
Korotkov's colleagues in Moscow at their daily
planning conference.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.510
The newspaper is one of the last truly critical
media outlets in Russia.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:33.280
For over 25 years Novaya Gazeta has been highly
regarded for its investigative articles into

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.850
corruption and human rights abuses.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:40.170
For years now, the journalists here have felt
the restrictions on press freedom in the country

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.330
tighten.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:45.760
Six of the paper's journalists have paid for
their reporting with their lives.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.770
- Including Anna Politkovskaya.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.950
She was murdered in 2006.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:55.030
Politkovskaya was known for her critical reporting
about the conflict in Chechnya.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:02:01.260
An element of fear has become part of everyday
life at Novaya Gazeta.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:12.760
“Our newspaper has lost as many journalists
as if we were reporting during wartime – even

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.870
though Russia is not at war.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.459
It's like working in a minefield.”

00:02:17.459 --> 00:02:24.150
"If you had to choose whether they should
send a sheep's head or come without warning

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:31.349
and murder someone, then I'd rather have a
severed sheep's head every single day."

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:34.840
The Head of the Russian Journalists' Union
on the other hand, says the bigger picture

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.880
when it comes to press freedom in Russia is
positive.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.900
"I think in Russia both the journalists and
the government are still learning how to communicate

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.730
with each other.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.690
And even though there are problems, there
is overreach, there are violations that verge

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:55.650
on censorship, nevertheless the situation
overall is improving.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:03:02.040
And, internationally speaking, the situation
in Russia is decent."

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.130
But to Denis Korotkov, his work certainly
feels dangerous.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:10.800
He sees the risk as a given, a normal part
of his investigative reporting that he is

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.599
willing to accept.

00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:15.850
Though it has meant that even his daughter
has been threatened.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:24.400
"I am interested in uncovering stories that
you can't see with the naked eye.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.300
Things that aren't right on the surface.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.900
Dealings that are secret are usually criminal
dealings.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:36.210
Of course, when you do this work you can take
on airs of "nothing can stop me."

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.920
But of course I have my limits.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:54.650
And God forbid if my opponents ever sound
out what those limits are."

